        ><span class="article-template__date">2025.09.13</span><h1
            class="article-template__title"
          >
            What is Irish Coffee? History, How to Make It, and Recommended Ways to Drink It 
          </h1>
        </header><div
            class="article-template__hero-container scroll-trigger animate--fade-in"
            
          >
            <div
              class="article-template__hero-adapt media"
              
                style="padding-bottom: 66.5%;"
              
            >
              <img
                srcset="
                  //bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009&width=350 350w,
                  //bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009&width=750 750w,
                  //bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009&width=1100 1100w,
                  //bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009&width=1500 1500w,
                  
                  
                  //bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009 2000w
                "
                sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1100px, (min-width: 750px) calc(100vw - 10rem), 100vw"
                src="//bongen-shirafushi-coffee.com/cdn/shop/articles/AdobeStock_798510186M_637ca882-4a66-40d3-afdf-fc88f5d50d58.jpg?v=1757663009&width=1100"
                loading="eager"
                fetchpriority="high"
                width="2000"
                height="1330"
                alt="アイリッシュコーヒーとは？歴史・作り方・おすすめの飲み方"
              >
            </div>
          </div><div
          class="article-template__content rte scroll-trigger animate--slide-in"
          
        ><p data-end="353" data-start="150"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> Irish coffee is one of the hot drinks that will warm your body and soul during the cold season. <br>This drink is an exquisite combination of the bitter coffee, the aroma of whiskey, and the mellow cream, creating a luxurious taste that is almost like dessert.</p>

<p data-end="353" data-start="150"> In this article, we will introduce in detail the appeal, origin, how to make, and recommended ways to drink Irish coffee.</p>

<p data-end="353" data-start="150"><meta charset="utf-8"> <span><section class="blogSection"></span> </p>

<h2 data-end="375" data-start="355">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-a4e43c05-7fff-70b6-613c-930e212df6b4"><span>What is Irish Coffee?</span></b>

</h2>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock"></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-img"> </p>

<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0909/8792/1706/files/pixta_119048686_M.jpg?v=1756265307" alt=""></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-body"></p>

<p data-end="415" data-start="377"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> An Irish coffee is a type of hot whiskey-based cocktail that generally consists of four ingredients:</p>

<p data-end="415" data-start="377"><meta charset="utf-8"> <div class="article-template__content__focus has-multiply-bg2"> </p>

<ul>

<li data-end="496" data-start="419">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-f8060310-7fff-e2b0-459d-2f18b91de95f"><span>Hot coffee</span></b>

</li>

 <li data-end="496" data-start="419"><b id="docs-internal-guid-f8060310-7fff-e2b0-459d-2f18b91de95f"><span>Irish whiskey</span></b></li>

<li data-end="496" data-start="419"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-f8060310-7fff-e2b0-459d-2f18b91de95f"><span>Sugar (brown sugar or granulated sugar)</span></b>
</li>

<li data-end="496" data-start="419"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-f8060310-7fff-e2b0-459d-2f18b91de95f"><span>Fresh cream (lightly whipped)</span><span><br></span></b>
</li>


</ul>

<p data-end="749" data-start="688"><meta charset="utf-8"></div></p>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>The layered appearance of these four ingredients in a glass is both beautiful and fragrant, making it <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>popular not only as a cocktail but also as a dessert drink</strong></span> .</span></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"> </p>

<h2 data-end="1223" data-start="1202">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<b id="docs-internal-guid-70579ddf-7fff-f187-91e0-8b7d4508276e"><span>History and origins</span></b>

</h2>

 <p dir="ltr"><span>Irish coffee is said to have originated in the 1940s at a restaurant at Shannon Airport in the west of Ireland.<br> At the time, this drink was invented by a restaurant chef to warm up American tourists stranded in bad weather.</span></p>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>This hot coffee with whiskey and cream on top was extremely popular and quickly spread all over the world. In the United States, <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>the cafe Buena Vista in San Francisco is said to have been particularly instrumental in its popularity</strong></span> .</span></p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"> </p>

<h2 data-end="1223" data-start="1202">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-fdb293c5-7fff-fe34-40af-72691c14d4b4"><span>The charm of Irish coffee</span></b><br>

</h2>

 <p dir="ltr"><span>The greatest appeal of Irish coffee is the temperature difference between the hot coffee and the cold cream, and the balance of alcohol and sweetness.<br> The first sip hits you with the smoothness of the cream, followed by the rich aroma of the whiskey, and finally the bitterness of the coffee. This trio <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>brings you a deep sense of satisfaction unlike any other cocktail</strong></span> .</span></p>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>Another fun thing about this drink is that the flavor changes dramatically depending on the type of coffee beans and whiskey used, so it's fun to try out different combinations to find your favorite.</span></p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"> </p>

<h2 data-end="773" data-start="751">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-554ee547-7fff-b8f3-6e9c-e673be0d41ff"><span>Basic recipe</span></b>

</h2>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock"></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-img"> </p>

<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0909/8792/1706/files/AdobeStock_1192273248M.jpg?v=1756265307" alt=""></p>

 <p></div></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-body"> </p>

<p data-start="367" data-end="485" class=""><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> You can now easily enjoy Irish coffee at home.<br> Here's a basic recipe:</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"> <span>Ingredients (for 1 cup)</span>
</h3>

<ul>

<li dir="ltr"> <span>Hot coffee: 120-150ml</span>
</li>

<li dir="ltr"> <span>Irish whiskey: 30ml</span>
</li>

<li dir="ltr"> <span>Sugar: 1-2 teaspoons (adjust to taste)</span>
</li>

<li dir="ltr"> <span>30ml fresh cream (lightly whipped)</span> </li>


</ul>

<p><b id="docs-internal-guid-82eaf2d5-7fff-734d-7e6e-6cd22db02b95"></b></p>

<p data-start="605" data-end="686" class=""><meta charset="utf-8"> <div class="article-template__content__focus has-multiply-bg2"> </p>

<p data-start="605" data-end="686" class=""><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> <b id="docs-internal-guid-1bb154d9-7fff-b6d9-aa2a-38c7f51aa0e7"><span>How to make it</span></b> <span></span></p>

<ol>

<li data-start="605" data-end="686" style="font-weight: bold;"> <strong>Heat a heat-resistant glass with hot water (to maintain the temperature).</strong>
</li>

<li data-start="605" data-end="686" style="font-weight: bold;"> <strong>Add hot coffee and sugar to a warmed glass and stir well to dissolve the sugar.</strong>
</li>

<li data-start="605" data-end="686" style="font-weight: bold;"> <strong>Add the whiskey and stir gently.</strong>
</li>

 <li data-start="605" data-end="686" style="font-weight: bold;"><strong>Finally, gently float the cream on top using the back of a spoon.</div></strong></li>


</ol>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>*The authentic way is to pour the cream on top without mixing it in. By carefully floating it on top with a spoon, you can create beautiful layers.</span></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"></p>

<h2 dir="ltr"> <span>Tips and variations on how to drink it</span>
</h2>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock"></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-img"> </p>

<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0909/8792/1706/files/AdobeStock_237862311M.jpg?v=1756265307" alt=""></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> <div class="blogSection-imgWithBlock-body"></p>

<h3 dir="ltr"> <span>If you want to enjoy the authentic style, don't mix it.</span>
</h3>

<p data-end="2204" data-start="2109"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> The authentic <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>way to drink Irish coffee is to keep the layers of the drink intact</strong></span> . <br>If you put your mouth to the glass and sip the coffee through the cream, you can enjoy a rich flavor that combines the mellowness of the cream, the bitterness of the coffee, and the richness of the whiskey. </p>

<h3 data-end="2218" data-start="2206">

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta charset="utf-8">Flavors change depending on the type of sugar</h3>

<p data-end="2290" data-start="2219"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> There is also room for creativity when it comes to the sugar used to add sweetness. If you want to add richness <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>, you can use brown sugar or cane sugar, which will give it a deeper flavor</strong></span> . If you want a lighter finish, granulated sugar is also fine.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"> <span>How to choose whiskey and coffee</span>
</h3>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>The whiskey used is basically Irish whiskey, but if you like a smoky flavor, you can substitute it with Scotch to create a unique taste.</span> <br>We also <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>recommend dark roast coffee,</strong></span> as its rich, bitter taste makes it easier to balance with the whiskey and cream.</p>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>We have a wide selection of dark roasted coffee beans that are perfect for Irish coffee. By choosing beans with a rich aroma and body, you can recreate the authentic taste at home.</span></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </div></p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"></p>

<h2 dir="ltr"> <span>Non-alcoholic versions also available</span>
</h2>

<p data-end="2204" data-start="2109"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"> For those who don't like alcohol or are concerned about drinking alcohol at night, <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>we also recommend a non-alcoholic version that uses whiskey-flavored syrup instead of whiskey.</strong></span> <br>You can enjoy the flavor without changing the appearance, making it perfect for cafe time with family and friends.</p>

<p> </section></p>

<p> <section class="blogSection"></p>

<h2 dir="ltr"> <span>Summary: Enrich your coffee time with a special cup</span>
</h2>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>Irish coffee is made with simple ingredients, but has a deep flavor and is a cup that makes the drinker feel special.<br> It's <span style="color: rgb(136, 41, 58);"><strong>perfect not only during the cold season, but also as a finishing touch to dinner or to enjoy while relaxing</strong></span> .</span></p>

<p dir="ltr"> <span>With just a little effort, you can turn your usual coffee time into a luxurious experience.<br> Please enjoy your own Irish coffee with your favorite coffee beans and whiskey.</span></p>

<p> </section></p>
        </div>
